WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.616
[MUSIC]

00:00:03.616 --> 00:00:06.471
LEAD is different from
other online courses,

00:00:06.471 --> 00:00:11.008
because it really gives you a lot in
terms of interaction with your peers,

00:00:11.008 --> 00:00:14.990
teaching assistants, but,
mostly, with the professors.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.140
That interaction with the professors,
to me,

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.630
is what completely sets LEAD
apart from other online courses.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:24.640
&gt;&gt; Never have I faced an issue where I
wanted to reach out to the faculty but

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:25.550
I was not able to.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.184
And they were pretty responsive, and

00:00:27.184 --> 00:00:31.410
kind enough to answer my
questions with elaborate answers.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.020
&gt;&gt; When I got exposed to the faculty
that Stanford is famous for,

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.280
it was beyond impressive.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.860
&gt;&gt; There's a lot of cases
where you have live sessions.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:42.630
And you can obviously
communicate that way.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.780
But there was also a lot of
discussions in the forums, or

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.955
even one on one email dialogs.

00:00:47.955 --> 00:00:52.340
And so you definitely had a lot a support
and you feel pretty connected to, and

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.390
engaged, and committed to the classes.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.964
&gt;&gt; You have access to this information,
and also this exchange is in such

00:00:58.964 --> 00:01:03.230
enriching experiences that any
other program did not experience.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:07.820
&gt;&gt; Often, I've actually used case studies
or questions that I got the day before or

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.600
that I saw the day before
in the lead program.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.608
And then I would come across something at
work and I could immediately apply it.

00:01:14.608 --> 00:01:18.990
&gt;&gt; The courses are designed such that they
give you the right tools, techniques and

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:22.060
framework, which you can take and
apply in your career.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.760
You can do it at your own pace.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.330
At your own convenient time.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:30.290
&gt;&gt; LEAD is probably the best learning
experience they can get outside an MBA,

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:34.820
if they're interested in learning about
business and leadership practices.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.960
&gt;&gt; It's not so
much about the certificate or the degree.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.002
It's much about the skills
that I acquire here.

